  "explanation": {
    "short": "These letters are the \"low class\": ม น ร ล ว ย ง (the smooth sounds) and also ค ช ท พ ฟ. A live syllable with a low-class first letter and no mark is also said in the plain mid tone, so มี, ยา and งาน sound level, just like ดี and ตา.",
    "more": "The sound of the letters: ม m, น n, ร r (a quick tap, often said like l), ล l, ว w, ย y, ง ng (as at the end of \"sing\", and it can also start a Thai word: งู). ค ช ท พ are k, ch, t and p with a puff of air, and ฟ is f. When no vowel is written between two consonants (นม, ลม, คน) the vowel is a short \"o\". The vowel ำ is \"am\". The class of the first letter matters from now on: the same mark or ending gives different tones for different classes."
  },
